This function safely copies a source string into a destination buffer, ensuring that the destination buffer is not overflowed. It first checks if the destination size is greater than zero to avoid accessing invalid memory. Then it uses `strncpy` to copy the source string into the destination buffer, stopping after `dest_size - 1` characters to leave space for the null terminator. Finally, it sets the null terminator at the end of the copied string.

